Package: organize
Version: 0.2.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Ivanadrian31 <ivanadrian31@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: 24
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: bash (>= 4.2)
Replaces: organize-dl
Conflicts: organize-dl
Homepage: https://github.com/Ivanadrian31/organize
Description: sort a directory into category subfolders
 organize moves the files of one directory into Images, Documents,
 Music, Videos, Archives and Others subfolders, chosen from the file
 extension. The default directory is the current one.
 .
 Only regular files directly inside the directory are touched; hidden
 files, subdirectories and symlinks are left alone. An existing file is
 never overwritten: a collision becomes name_1.ext, name_2.ext and so
 on. A --preview flag prints the plan without moving anything, and
 --images, --documents, --music, --videos, --archives and --others
 restrict a run to one or more categories.
 .
 System directories and the root of a git repository are refused, and
 files that a download manager is still writing are skipped.
